dmin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes [Proposal #15460](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15460)\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<del>Adjusting `light_temperature` will directly set the `light_color` to the target color. But you can still manually adjust `light_color`.  </del>\r\n\r\n<del>This logic is different from the logic when `physical unit lights` is enabled, because in fact you can set a light's color to pure white when `physical unit lights` is disabled, but a color from temperature can't be pure white. So intuitively, there seems nothing wrong to me with this interaction method, but I feel there might be a better way🥲. I will modify if anyone can tell me a better way.</del>\r\n\r\n<img width=\"273\" height=\"65\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/21300140-ed19-4a7c-8a48-a95af9114abb\" />\r\n\r\nI apologize for hastily submitting this PR without having fully thought it through.\r\n\r\nI felt the previous implementation was unreasonable, so I modified it. Now whether to multiply the temperature color to the original color is decided by a toggle. This toggle will only be shown when `use_physical_light_units` is disabled in Project Settings. Now it behaves the same as when `use_physical_light_units` is enabled if you turn it on. \r\n\r\n<img width=\"470\" height=\"98\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8d708e49-2a0f-410a-af56-1cdb8edfa355\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"505\" height=\"119\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01b7e124-07d5-45a5-aea2-43380f0c2087\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"488\" height=\"80\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2fb8193d-eba6-49ab-8c4e-e668aa72f3ef\" />\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","re